      "bullets": [
        "POSIX shell colon (`:`) evaluates parameter expansions like `${VAR:=default}` to set default variables without executing external binaries.",
        "In Bash and POSIX scripts, `:` functions as a built-in alias for `true`, optimizing `while :; do` loops and placeholder branches.",
        "Use `: > file.txt` for fast, allocation-free file truncation, or for evaluating multi-line string blocks without executing code."
